================================================================================
NOTICE — what this licence does and does not cover
================================================================================

The MIT licence above applies to the samjho source code and to the material this
project authored: the ingestion and retrieval code, the web application, the
concept animations and explainers, the quizzes, and the syllabus structure data
in `data/syllabus/`.

It does NOT apply to textbook content, because no textbook content is included
here.

- No NCERT textbook PDF, and no text extracted from one, is distributed with
  this repository. Textbook text is not part of the software and is not
  licensed by it.
- Textbook content remains the property of its rights holders and is governed by
  their terms, not by this licence. NCERT's terms of use restrict republication
  and prohibit hosting their books as part of a website, service or software
  package. See `docs/adr/ADR-001-licensing-boundary.md`.
- A samjho instance operates on a copy of a textbook that the person running it
  supplies locally. That copy stays on their machine, in a gitignored `corpus/`
  directory, and is never redistributed by this project.
- Any material under `data/demo-corpus/` is third-party content under its own open licence — currently
  Wikipedia text under CC BY-SA 4.0 — and that licence governs those files, not this one. Each file's
  source URL, licence, retrieval date and hash is recorded in `data/demo-corpus/SOURCES.md`, and
  attribution is repeated in each file's header. CC BY-SA is a share-alike licence: it is not the same
  as CC BY, and redistributing modified versions of that text carries its share-alike condition.
- Answers generated by samjho are machine-generated prose produced from
  retrieved text. They are not quotations from any book and must not be
  presented as such.
